CONFORMANT — the judge should return an empty violation list.

Judged against rule-authoring.md and cc-artifacts.md, every required element is present AND does the
work it exists to do:

  - The numbered clause states a testable obligation in MUST grammar ("MUST be derived from — or
    asserted against — the authoritative enumeration"), with an explicit BLOCKED disposition. A
    reviewer can say of any given diff whether it complies.
  - The DO / DO-NOT block shows two runnable forms that behave DIFFERENTLY on the same input: a
    `comm` against a derived member list, versus fixture cases restating the prefixes. The pair
    demonstrates the distinction rather than restating the prose.
  - BLOCKED rationalizations are an enumerated corpus of verbatim phrases an agent's own reasoning
    could match against, including the parenthetical rebuttal on the last entry.
  - Both `**Why:**` lines are two sentences and name the failure mode (agreement by construction)
    rather than restating the clause.
  - Frontmatter, Wiring block and Origin are present and internally consistent; Origin cites a
    specific incident with concrete numbers.

Discriminator. This file and its paired candidate share frontmatter, the `##` heading skeleton, the
numbered-clause count, a Wiring block, an Origin section, and sit within 1.5x of each other in size.
Shape therefore cannot separate them — the pair is separable only by reading what the furniture
CONTAINS. A judge that scores this pair by checking which file has more sections is measuring
formatting and will get it wrong.
